Three working diagrams of how this project fits together, straight from the project's own planning docs, unedited. Colors are the same CityLink yellow, purple, and cream the site itself uses, pulled from the bus's own livery.

Two other operations diagrams from the same set are internal-only per the public-surface rule and aren't posted here; the operator may override that call.

**How someone becomes a member**, from application through to active (or not).

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/member-lifecycle.svg" alt="Member lifecycle: submit application, verify email, keyholder claims and tours, one keyholder decides, then assent leads to active, paused, left, or removed." />

**What happens after you're active.** Contributions and other extras stay optional, and separate from membership itself.

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/member-projection-flow.svg" alt="Member projection flow: active membership branches into an optional contribution offer (no contribution, cash or check, or Stripe when live gates pass) and an optional projection queue for mailing list and mailbox, none of which change membership." />

**How a tool moves** from the shelf to your hands and back.

<img src="/diagrams/launch-member-v0/inventory-custody-flow.svg" alt="Inventory custody flow: scan a tool, check its availability and condition, finalize a loan, then scan it back in, inspect it, and route it to available or quarantine." />
